Z||000008||Standard||04-27-2001||11:06 PM||||I'm sure I don't need the pair.  Actually, just took them off of my Kona full-suspension bruiser to put on a pair of Primo flat pedals.  I mainly use the bike for urban assaults and just screwin' around, so the spd's were just a hindrance.  Check out  <A HREF="http://www.666bmx.com" TARGET=_blank>www.666bmx.com</A> .  Webpage our riding group is making about the local riding scene.  Here's me:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.666bmx.com/4-08-01nightride9a.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.666bmx.com/nightride06.jpg">  <P>Not the best pics but you get the idea   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>got your mail hoop<P><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||14
